%N A399802 Squarefree numbers with four prime factors whose positive divisors have inclusion-maximal Sidon subsets of nonconsecutive sizes.
%C A399802 A Sidon subset is a subset whose unordered sums of two not necessarily distinct elements are all different. It is inclusion-maximal if no further element can be adjoined while preserving this property.
%C A399802 For every squarefree m with at most three prime factors, the sizes of the inclusion-maximal Sidon subsets of the positive divisors of m are consecutive.
%C A399802 The first gaps occur for four prime factors. If m = p*q*r*s with p < q < r < s prime and the sizes are not consecutive, then m belongs to one of six explicit algebraic families; see Huber link.
%H A399802 Felix Huber, <a href="https://felixhuber-math.github.io/papers/sunflower-classification-sidon-spectra-four-prime-divisor-sets.pdf">A Sunflower Classification of Gaps in Maximal Sidon Spectra of Four-Prime Divisor Sets</a>.
%H A399802 Felix Huber, <a href="/A399802/a399802.txt">Maple program</a>
%e A399802 17255 = 5717*29 is a term because the inclusion-maximal Sidon subsets of its positive divisors have sizes 10, 11, 12, and 14, but not 13.
%p A399802 # See Huber link.
